    "c5_counterfactual_stable": "A counterfactual A/B was run in this context AND its CONCLUSION reproduced across two independent 400-game batches. For the damage-counter context the reproduced conclusion is 'no variant improvement' (LCB not > 0 in both batches); point estimates are noise-dominated (sign-flipping), but the no-improvement conclusion is stable. Contexts without any counterfactual A/B cannot satisfy c5. 'Stable' therefore means a completed, reproducible counterfactual verdict \u2014 NOT that a variant is stably better.",
